.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-START" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-start - Start recording the terminal session you are attached to


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings start [session-id] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Start recording the terminal session that a pb connect on this computer is attached to.
Everyone attached sees a REC mark while it records. The session ID is optional; name it when
you are attached to more than one session.

.PP
Only admins start recordings (on a personal machine, its owner). The machine needs a recording
key (set up in the console under Terminals > Recordings) and a team also needs the Teams plan;
a refusal says which condition is missing.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for start

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recordings start
  pb recordings start S123 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings(1)\fP
